-- title:
--   Descent of translation-invariant power series along a formal isogeny
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative Noetherian ring, $n$ a natural number, and let $F$ and $F'$ be $n$-dimensional formal group laws over $B$, each given by an $n$-tuple of power series in the $2n$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,n$ with zero constant term, with linear coefficients in the left and right blocks equal to $\delta_{ij}$, and satisfying the associativity identity; both are assumed commutative, i.e. interchanging the two blocks of variables fixes each component. Let $\rho = (\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ be power series in $B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ with $\rho_i(0)=0$ which form a homomorphism from $F$ to $F'$, in the sense that substituting $F$ into $\rho_i$ equals substituting $(\rho(x),\rho(y))$ into the $i$-th component of $F'$. Assume there is $N$ with $x_i^N \in (\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ for every $i$, and that the quotient $B[\![x]\!]/(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ is finite and projective as a $B$-module. Then for every $G \in B[\![x]\!]$ such that $G(F(x,y)) - G(x)$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y]\!]$ generated by $\rho_1(y),\dots,\rho_n(y)$, there exists $H \in B[\![x]\!]$ with $G = H(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ and $H(0) = G(0)$.
--
--   This is the descent statement for an isogeny $\rho : F \to F'$ of commutative formal groups with finite projective kernel: a power series invariant under translation by the kernel is a power series in the $\rho_i$. It is obtained from the corresponding statement over a local base by localising, and is used together with the injectivity of substitution by $\rho$ in the construction of homomorphisms of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_eq_subst_of_subst_toPowerSeries_sub_mem_span_of_X_pow_mem_span.lean

